The '''Nobody Party''' ('''NP'''), whose supporters are commonly called '''Nobodies''', is an [[Balisca]]n youth-oriented [[w:Radical politics|radical]] and [[w:counterculture|countercultural]] [[w:revolution|revolutionary]] {{W|joke party}}, effectively an offshoot of the [[Anarchism in Balisca|Baliscan anti-statist movement]]. It was founded on 22 November 1973. They employed theatrical gestures to mock the social, political and economic {{W|status quo}}. They have been described as a highly theatrical, {{W|anti-authoritarian}} and anarchist youth movement of "symbolic politics".

Since they are well known for {{W|street theatre}} and politically themed {{W|pranks}}, they are often associated with the wider ''[[Desconexión]]'' subculture. The Nobody Party has expressed solidarity with the {{W|CrimethInc}} collective, and the [[Toju|/toju]] {{W|hacktivism|hacktivist}} bloc. 

